{"type": "thinking", "text": "Fraud level 10.31% >8.3%, so applies \">8.3%\" plus null. Monthly volume 100k-1m.\n\nNow fees. We need determine candidate fee rules matching merchant and transaction. Let's build matcher and evaluate fraud transactions for each ACI A-G. Need handle account_type: [] wildcard; capture_delay merchant \"1\" -> likely \"<3\" (or maybe \"immediate\"?). Capture delay \"1\" means number of days capture from auth to settlement: 1 day, which is <3. Rule capture_delay null applies too.\n\nMCC 5942 (books). Check fee MCC lists containing 5942? The unique MCC lists none include 5942! Lists: 8000..., 8062..., 4111..., 5734/5735/5736/5816/5912/7399/5964/5999, 5814..., 5411..., 3000... No 5942. Hmm. If merchant_category_code list must contain merchant MCC, then no fee rules apply to Belles via MCC (unless [] wildcard). There are 127 rules with MCC [] wildcard. That's likely intentional: MCC wildcard rules are the only ones for Belles. If [] means applies all MCC. Good.\n\nSimilarly account_type [] wildcard.\n\nWe need verify rule matching semantics from tasks 1681/1753 perhaps. But no oracle. Let's compute for Belles.\n\nLet's write script to list matching rules for a representative fraudulent transaction under assumptions, count by scheme etc. For each ACI candidate and each transaction, match rules based on: card_scheme equal, account_type contains R or empty, capture_delay compatible, monthly_fraud_level matches >8.3% or null, monthly_volume matches 100k-1m or null, MCC [] or contains 5942, is_credit matches True/null, aci [] or contains candidate, intracountry matches False/null.\n\nWe need define date? No date in fee rules. capture_delay \"1\": possible mapping. We'll test <3, immediate, null-only, etc.\n\nLet's compute. Interpret cost. First list matching rules counts and fee ranges."}
{"type": "tool_call", "callId": "call_00_rRBF51cZ9vIdtpPmtFIU4343", "tool": "bash", "input": {"command": "python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, csv, collections\nfees=json.load(open('inputs/fees.json'))\nrows=[]\nwith open('inputs/payments.csv', newline='') as f:\n    for x in csv.DictReader(f):\n        if x['merchant']=='Belles_cookbook_store' and x['year']=='2023' and 1<=int(x['day_of_year'])<=31 and x['has_fraudulent_dispute']=='True':\n            rows.append(x)\n\ndef in_interval(val, s):\n    if s is None: return True\n    v=float(val)\n    if s.startswith('<'): return v < float(s[1:].rstrip('%').rstrip('m').rstrip('k')) if s.endswith('%') else None\n    # implement separately\n\ndef match_monthly_fraud(level, rule):\n    # level percent\n    if rule is None: return True\n    if rule=='>8.3%': return level > 8.3\n    if rule=='<7.2%': return level < 7.2\n    lo,hi=rule.rstrip('%').split('-')\n    return float(lo) <= level <= float(hi)\ndef match_volume(vol, rule):\n    if rule is None: return True\n    if rule=='>5m': return vol > 5_000_000\n    if rule=='1m-5m': return 1_000_000 <= vol <= 5_000_000\n    if rule=='100k-1m': return 100_000 <= vol <= 1_000_000\n    if rule=='<100k': return vol < 100_000\n    raise ValueError(rule)\n\ndef match(r, t, aci, capdelay):\n    if r['card_scheme']!=t['card_scheme']: return False\n    if r['account_type'] and 'R' not in r['account_type']: return False\n    # capture delay\n    if r['capture_delay'] is not None and r['capture_delay']!=capdelay: return False\n    if not match_monthly_fraud(10.313064352048135, r['monthly_fraud_level']): return False\n    if not match_volume(113260.42, r['monthly_volume']): return False\n    if r['merchant_category_code'] and 5942 not in r['merchant_category_code']: return False\n    if r['is_credit'] is not None and bool(r['is_credit'])!= (t['is_credit']=='True'): return False\n    if r['aci'] and aci not in r['aci']: return False\n    intra = (t['issuing_country']==t['acquirer_country'])\n    if r['intracountry'] is not None and bool(r['intracountry'])!=intra: return False\n    return True\n\nfor cap in ['<3','immediate','3-5','>5','manual']:\n    print('\\nCAP',cap)\n    for aci in 'ABCDEFG':\n        total=0; cnt=0; byscheme=collections.Counter(); rules_by_scheme=collections.defaultdict(list)\n        for t in rows:\n            rs=[r for r in fees if match(r,t,aci,cap)]\n            if rs:\n                # average across matching rules\n                ff=[r['fixed_amount']+r['rate']*float(t['eur_amount'])/10000 for r in rs]\n                total += sum(ff)/len(ff)\n                cnt += 1\n                byscheme[t['card_scheme']] += sum(ff)/len(ff)\n                rules_by_scheme[t['card_scheme']].append((t['psp_reference'],len(rs),min(ff),max(ff)))\n        print(aci, 'tx matched',cnt,'total',round(total,2), 'by scheme', {k:round(v,2) for k,v in byscheme.items()})\nEOF", "description": "Compute total fees per ACI scenario with average rules"}}
