{"type": "thinking", "text": "Still >8.3%, 100k-1m. No impact.\n\nWhat about monthly volume bracket boundaries: 113k is 100k-1m. Good.\n\nNow, another major ambiguity: fee rule applicability for monthly_volume/monthly_fraud. For a *single hypothetical transaction*, do you use merchant's monthly volume/fraud level? Yes question says Belles in January. We used. Capture delay \"1\" -> <3.\n\nWhat if fee rules with monthly_fraud_level \"<7.2%\" etc are evaluated against *each transaction's* fraud? No, monthly.\n\nNow, \"move the fraudulent transactions towards a different ACI\" could also change the monthly fraud level? No.\n\nLet's compute exact totals for B under various aggregation and capture mapping."}
{"type": "tool_call", "callId": "call_00_HadkrDmjHH2QjZEmonQn0786", "tool": "bash", "input": {"command": "python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, csv\nfrom decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP\nfees=json.load(open('inputs/fees.json'))\nrows=[]\nwith open('inputs/payments.csv', newline='') as f:\n    for x in csv.DictReader(f):\n        if x['merchant']=='Belles_cookbook_store' and x['year']=='2023' and 1<=int(x['day_of_year'])<=31 and x['has_fraudulent_dispute']=='True':\n            rows.append(x)\ndef mf(level, rule):\n    if rule is None: return True\n    if rule=='>8.3%': return level>8.3\n    if rule=='<7.2%': return level<7.2\n    lo,hi=rule[:-1].split('-');return float(lo.rstrip('%'))<=level<=float(hi.rstrip('%'))\ndef mv(v,rule):\n    if rule is None: return True\n    return {'>5m':v>5e6,'1m-5m':1e6<=v<=5e6,'100k-1m':1e5<=v<=1e6,'<100k':v<1e5}[rule]\ndef match(r,t,aci,cap):\n    if r['card_scheme']!=t['card_scheme']: return False\n    if r['account_type'] and 'R' not in r['account_type']: return False\n    if r['capture_delay'] is not None and r['capture_delay']!=cap: return False\n    if not mf(10.313064352048135,r['monthly_fraud_level']): return False\n    if not mv(113260.42,r['monthly_volume']): return False\n    if r['merchant_category_code'] and 5942 not in r['merchant_category_code']: return False\n    if r['is_credit'] is not None and bool(r['is_credit'])!=(t['is_credit']=='True'): return False\n    if r['aci'] and aci not in r['aci']: return False\n    if r['intracountry'] is not None and bool(r['intracountry'])!=(t['issuing_country']==t['acquirer_country']): return False\n    return True\nfor aci in 'ABCDEFG':\n    total=0; cnt=0\n    for t in rows:\n        ff=[r['fixed_amount']+r['rate']*float(t['eur_amount'])/10000 for r in fees if match(r,t,aci,'<3')]\n        if ff:\n            total+=sum(ff)/len(ff);cnt+=1\n    print(aci,cnt,repr(total),round(total,2), 'avg',round(total/cnt,4) if cnt else None)\nEOF", "description": "Get exact ACI totals and means"}}
{"type": "tool_result", "callId": "call_00_HadkrDmjHH2QjZEmonQn0786", "status": "completed", "result": "A 94 89.82079225 89.82 avg 0.9555\nB 94 77.87079725000001 77.87 avg 0.8284\nC 94 88.70913825000001 88.71 avg 0.9437\nD 44 52.323496 52.32 avg 1.1892\nE 44 41.6610305 41.66 avg 0.9468\nF 30 47.305032000000004 47.31 avg 1.5768\nG 30 61.05101400000001 61.05 avg 2.035\n"}
