3.94, TransactPlus=36.02.\nThen answer \"NexPay:3.49\" if format card_scheme: fee and \"preferred choice\" is card scheme. That's another candidate. But question explicitly says ACI.\n\nMaybe the format `{card_scheme}:{fee}` is a copy-paste error from a related question where answer is card_scheme. The parent asks to focus on this. We should explain: if literal, the only scheme-level interpretation is not sensible because the question asks ACI; the format is likely erroneous. Recommended answer `B:77.87` (ACI: total fee). Alternative `B:0.83` (mean per fraud transaction), `E:41.66` (partial coverage naive sum), and possibly `NexPay:3.49` if format literally demands card_scheme and we optimize scheme per ACI.\n\nNeed compute exact per scheme values and maybe totals. Let's get exact with full precision. Also check B total 77.87079725 -> 77.87. B mean = 0.8284 -> 0.83. E total 41.6610305 -> 41.66. NexPay under C =? Let's compute exact. Also maybe the single best ACI per card_scheme and associated cost.\n\nLet's run script to produce exact table."}
{"type": "tool_call", "callId": "call_00_kp8YHxwEtyhrr9WEjDs43219", "tool": "bash", "input": {"command": "python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, csv, collections\nfees=json.load(open('inputs/fees.json'))\nrows=[]\nwith open('inputs/payments.csv', newline='') as f:\n    for x in csv.DictReader(f):\n        if x['merchant']=='Belles_cookbook_store' and x['year']=='2023' and 1<=int(x['day_of_year'])<=31 and x['has_fraudulent_dispute']=='True':\n            rows.append(x)\n\ndef mf(level, rule):\n    if rule is None: return True\n    if rule=='>8.3%': return level>8.3\n    if rule=='<7.2%': return level<7.2\n    lo,hi=rule[:-1].split('-'); return float(lo.rstrip('%'))<=level<=float(hi.rstrip('%'))\ndef mv(v,rule):\n    if rule is None: return True\n    return {'>5m':v>5e6,'1m-5m':1e6<=v<=5e6,'100k-1m':1e5<=v<=1e6,'<100k':v<1e5}[rule]\ndef match(r,t,aci,cap='<3'):\n    if r['card_scheme']!=t['card_scheme']: return False\n    if r['account_type'] and 'R' not in r['account_type']: return False\n    if r['capture_delay'] is not None and r['capture_delay']!=cap: return False\n    if not mf(10.313064352048135,r['monthly_fraud_level']): return False\n    if not mv(113260.42,r['monthly_volume']): return False\n    if r['merchant_category_code'] and 5942 not in r['merchant_category_code']: return False\n    if r['is_credit'] is not None and bool(r['is_credit'])!=(t['is_credit']=='True'): return False\n    if r['aci'] and aci not in r['aci']: return False\n    if r['intracountry'] is not None and bool(r['intracountry'])!=(t['issuing_country']==t['acquirer_country']): return False\n    return True\n\ntable={}\nfor aci in 'ABCDEFG':\n    by=collections.defaultdict(float); n=collections.Counter()\n    for t in rows:\n        ff=[r['fixed_amount']+r['rate']*float(t['eur_amount'])/10000 for r in fees if match(r,t,aci)]\n        if ff:\n            by[t['card_scheme']]+=sum(ff)/len(ff); n[t['card_scheme']]+=1\n    table[aci]=(by,n)\n    print(aci, 'total',repr(sum(by.values())), 'n',sum(n.values()), {k:(n[k],repr(by[k])) for k in by})\nprint('\\nBest ACI per scheme (all-coverage only A/B/C):')\nfor s in ['GlobalCard','NexPay','SwiftCharge','TransactPlus']:\n    opts={a:table[a][0][s] for a in 'ABC' if table[a][1][s]>0}\n    best=min(opts,key=opts.get)\n    print(s,best,repr(opts[best]),'allopts',{a:round(v,4) for a,v in opts.items()})\nprint('\\nPer scheme any ACI incl partial:')\nfor s in ['GlobalCard','NexPay','SwiftCharge','TransactPlus']:\n    opts={a:table[a][0][s] for a in 'ABCDEFG' if table[a][1][s]>0}\n    best=min(opts,key=opts.get)\n    print(s,best,repr(opts[best]),{a:(table[a][1][s],round(v,4)) for a,v in opts.items()})\nEOF", "description": "Exact per-scheme and per-ACI fee tables"}}
